gt; Signed-off-by: Kalle Valo &lt;kvalo@qca.qualcomm.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/322620 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Peter Oh &lt;poh@qca.qualcomm.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="322620" owner_email="poh@qca.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/20/322620/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I44031e9f904c2af44a5ed7bcc78cd852c1fac928" commit="d0cc00dbd1e9231c29cb7cc5502504b1a098b246" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ath10k: set peer MFP flag in peer assoc command  Set peer's management frame protection flag in peer assoc command, this setting will enable/disable encrytion of management frames in fw.  Setting of this flag is based on whether MFP is enabled/disabled at STA and a firmware feature flag ATH10K_FW_FEATURE_MFP_SUPPORT. This is because only firmwares 10.1.561 and above have support for MFP.  (cherry picked from commit &quot;90eceb3b5fb0d0f413f475165314d4578c3a46c4&quot;) (source: git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/kvalo/ath.git)  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49352 TEST=build/boot on Arkham and verified iperf throughput.  Change-Id: I44031e9f904c2af44a5ed7bcc78cd852c1fac928 Signed-off-by: Tamizh chelvam &lt;c_traja@qti.qualcomm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Manikanta pubbisetty &lt;c_mpubbi@qti.qualcomm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Kalle Valo &lt;kvalo@qca.qualcomm.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/322621 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Peter Oh &lt;poh@qca.qualcomm.com&gt; Tested-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Julan Hsu &lt;julanhsu@google.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="322621" owner_email="poh@qca.qualcomm.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/21/322621/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If602c477692e6a862db4e3ed432fc890ec410bdd" commit="d71625b451c45808da9ced96212f80856af2f1b4" commit_message="[autotest] Fix a bug for nightly run in suite scheduler  suite scheduler parses the config file in every loop (about 5min), and merge the new config to the existing ones. During the merge, deadline is updated. CL 323331 changed the logic of nightly run for it to be able to trigger at every hour. This also change how deadline should be updated.  The deadline should be unchanged in merge, otherwise the deadline will be changed to the next hour, thus no nightly run will be scheduled as deadline will always be pushed an hour in the future.  This change removes the Merge override in Nightly class so the dealine can stay unchanged during Merge.  BUG=chromium:581113 TEST=local run, unittest  Change-Id: If602c477692e6a862db4e3ed432fc890ec410bdd Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324100 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Kevin Cheng &lt;kevcheng@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="324100" owner_email="dshi@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/00/324100/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I8cfcddac54aa9514c0f4de1f35ebd8f2fae229c1" commit="fd433b8bff00a9585d0fa2838a99befbdd80991b" commit_message="CHROMIUM: config: Enable multiple IPv6 routing tables  For various security reasons, third party VPNs do not tunnel all system network traffic; they only tunnel traffic owned by the chronos user.  chronos traffic is diverted to a separate routing table by firewalld using `ip rule` and iptables XT_MATCH_OWNER.  Currently this is only enabled for IPv4 traffic.  It should be enabled for both IPv4 and IPv6.  The first step in making this happen is to enable kernel support for multiple IPv6 routing tables on all platforms.  BUG=chromium:522003 TEST=build samus and veyron_minnie kernels; manually verify option is set  Change-Id: I8cfcddac54aa9514c0f4de1f35ebd8f2fae229c1 Signed-off-by: Kevin Cernekee &lt;cernekee@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323406 Reviewed-by: Filipe Brandenburger &lt;filbranden@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bartosz Fabianowski &lt;bartfab@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323406" owner_email="cernekee@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/06/323406/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iab43619d629885b14792962b0182ba27b182a850" commit="b161b2ab642ee25d0cce393a86efad2f04ed4a53" commit_message="[autotest] Log time used to run autoupdater for CrOS  The stats data will be used to monitor the overall history of time used to run AU and Paygen test.  BUG=chromium:561036 TEST=None  Change-Id: Iab43619d629885b14792962b0182ba27b182a850 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323397 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Alex Deymo &lt;deymo@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="323397" owner_email="dshi@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/97/323397/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3b1f461771b6ed24d